// file as the bytes it encodes. A file is named by a hash of its key, never by the key itself,
// so no key (`../`, `/`, an empty one, one too long for a file name) can name a file outside
// the store's directory; the key is kept inside the entry, ahead of the bytes, so `keys()`
// answers it and two keys sharing a hash stay apart. An entry is written to a partial file and
// renamed into place, so a write cut short never leaves half an entry, and the store runs one
// call at a time. Everything kept is removed whenever a session ends -- a logout, an expiry
// nothing renews, and before a login starts a new one -- and at start-up when the app signs
// people in and holds no session, so a second account never reads what the first kept.

